# Code this repo commits but the map is NOT meant to describe.
#
# `eval/fixtures/trapdoor/` is a synthetic codebase built to TRIP coyodex's own advisories —
# broken anchors, overclaimed edges, an oversized flat folder, a generated dir. Left in the
# analysed tree it would inflate the weight map, skew the component expectation E, and show up
# forever as an unreferenced directory in coyodex's self-map. It is not part of the product.
#
# The trailing entries cover the artifacts a build OVER the fixture writes back into it
# (`.coyodex/` is already a built-in exclusion, but the fixture's own map/eval dirs are named
# here so a reader of this file can see the whole story in one place).
eval/fixtures/trapdoor/
